---
import DocLayout from '../../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
---

<DocLayout title="SDKs">
  <h1>SDKs</h1>
  <p>
    Driftstack ships first-party SDKs for TypeScript and Python; Go is planned. All SDKs expose
    identical resource shapes (sessions, api-keys, profiles, webhooks, billing, auth, account)
    generated from the same Zod single source of truth in
    <code>@driftstack/api-types</code>.
  </p>

  <div class="not-prose mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
    <article class="rounded-md border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500">TypeScript</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm font-medium text-slate-900">@driftstack/sdk</p>
      <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-xs text-slate-600">npm install @driftstack/sdk</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-500">Status: live</p>
    </article>
    <article class="rounded-md border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500">Python</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm font-medium text-slate-900">driftstack</p>
      <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-xs text-slate-600">pip install driftstack</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-500">Status: live</p>
    </article>
    <article class="rounded-md border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500">Go</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm font-medium text-slate-900">driftstack-go</p>
      <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-xs text-slate-600">go get github.com/driftstackdev/...</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-500">Status: planned</p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <h2>Reference</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/sdk/versioning/">Versioning policy</a> — how SDKs version independently of the
      HTTP API, deprecation rules, CHANGELOG conventions.
    </li>
  </ul>
</DocLayout>
